      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZEPHIRINE (1) has the strongest overall case after a Quality second at this track and a dominant Open win over Yalla at this venue the run prior. She is proven at 1450m, has an excellent track-and-distance profile and comes back into BM65 company with enough recent substance to absorb the big weight. THE WELLIAN (6) is the main danger on consistency around this course and distance, with genuine weight relief after a sound BM50 fourth at Cloncurry, though the earlier margin behind DARK HARMONY keeps him honest. DARK HARMONY (2) has a strong claim for the multiples after winning a BM60 here by six and a half lengths, and his wide run when fourth in Open grade at Cloncurry reads better than the bare result. REGAL JUDGEMENT (3) ran below expectations last time at Charleville over 1625m, finishing fourth. Goes well at this journey with two wins from six starts and is sure to play a big role.",
